    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic. It does not compute an exact optimum.\n\n**Approach**\n\n1. **Coverage test.** A router at (a, b) covers (x, y) only if the rectangle between them has no wall. This splits cleanly by row:\n   - Scan rows outward from the router, going up and then down.\n   - In each row, keep a running minimum of how far you can go left and right before hitting a wall.\n   - With precomputed \"non-wall run length\" arrays, one router's coverage is a list of at most 2R+1 row segments.\n   - Coverage is symmetric: A covers B exactly when B covers A.\n\n2. **Initial gains.** For every non-wall cell, compute how many target cells a router there would cover. Row prefix sums make this about 4R operations per cell.\n\n3. **Greedy selection.** Pick routers by the ratio `newly covered targets / (Pr + Pb \u00b7 dist)`, highest first.\n   - `dist` is the Chebyshev distance to the nearest cell already on the backbone. Any cell type can carry backbone, so linking a router costs exactly `dist` new cells.\n   - The candidates live in a lazy max-heap. When a popped entry's ratio has gone stale, it is pushed back with the new value.\n   - When a cell's backbone distance shrinks, a new heap entry is pushed for it.\n   - A router is placed only if it fits in the remaining budget and gains more than it costs (`1000\u00b7gain > cost`).\n\n4. **Updating after each placement.**\n   - **Gains:** for each newly covered target cell, decrement the gain of every candidate that covers it, using the symmetry.\n   - **Backbone:** lay a straight 8-connected path from the router to its nearest backbone cell. Then update the distance field with an incremental multi-source BFS from the new path cells.\n\n5. **Output.** Backbone cells are listed in the order they were added. Each path is listed from the existing backbone outward, so every cell has an earlier neighbour. Total spending never exceeds B.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint H,W,R,Pb,Pr; long long B; int br,bc;\nvector<string> g;\nvector<unsigned char> rrun, lrun; // non-wall runs to right/left, capped R+1\nvector<int> gainv;\nvector<char> covered;\n\ntemplate<class F> inline void forCover(int a,int b,F f){\n    for(int dir=1;dir>=-1;dir-=2){\n        int limL=R,limR=R;\n        for(int i=0;i<=R;i++){\n            int r=a+dir*i; if(r<0||r>=H) break;\n            int idx=r*W+b;\n            int lr=(int)rrun[idx]-1, ll=(int)lrun[idx]-1;\n            if(lr<0) break;\n            limR=min(limR,lr); limL=min(limL,ll);\n            if(dir==-1&&i==0) continue;\n            f(r,b-limL,b+limR);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstruct E{double v;int cell;int ver;};\nstruct Cmp{bool operator()(const E&a,const E&b)const{ if(a.v!=b.v) return a.v<b.v; return a.cell>b.cell;}};\n\nint main(){\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\",&H,&W,&R);\n    scanf(\"%d %d %lld\",&Pb,&Pr,&B);\n    scanf(\"%d %d\",&br,&bc);\n    g.resize(H);\n    {\n        static char buf[2000];\n        for(int i=0;i<H;i++){ scanf(\"%s\",buf); g[i]=buf; if((int)g[i].size()<W) g[i].resize(W,'-'); }\n    }\n    int N=H*W;\n    rrun.assign(N,0); lrun.assign(N,0);\n    for(int r=0;r<H;r++){\n        for(int c=W-1;c>=0;c--){\n            if(g[r][c]=='#') rrun[r*W+c]=0;\n            else { int nx=(c+1<W)?rrun[r*W+c+1]:0; rrun[r*W+c]=(unsigned char)min(R+1,nx+1);}\n        }\n        for(int c=0;c<W;c++){\n            if(g[r][c]=='#') lrun[r*W+c]=0;\n            else { int nx=(c>0)?lrun[r*W+c-1]:0; lrun[r*W+c]=(unsigned char)min(R+1,nx+1);}\n        }\n    }\n    vector<int> pre((size_t)H*(W+1),0);\n    for(int r=0;r<H;r++) for(int c=0;c<W;c++) pre[r*(W+1)+c+1]=pre[r*(W+1)+c]+(g[r][c]=='.');\n    gainv.assign(N,0); covered.assign(N,0);\n    for(int a=0;a<H;a++) for(int b=0;b<W;b++){\n        if(g[a][b]=='#') continue;\n        int s=0;\n        forCover(a,b,[&](int r,int l,int rr){ s+=pre[r*(W+1)+rr+1]-pre[r*(W+1)+l]; });\n        gainv[a*W+b]=s;\n    }\n    vector<int> dist(N), src(N);\n    int s0=br*W+bc;\n    for(int r=0;r<H;r++) for(int c=0;c<W;c++){\n        dist[r*W+c]=max(abs(r-br),abs(c-bc)); src[r*W+c]=s0;\n    }\n    vector<char> isBB(N,0); isBB[s0]=1;\n    vector<int> ver(N,0);\n    priority_queue<E,vector<E>,Cmp> pq;\n    auto costOf=[&](int p)->long long{ return (long long)Pr+(long long)Pb*dist[p]; };\n    for(int p=0;p<N;p++){\n        if(gainv[p]>0) pq.push({(double)gainv[p]/costOf(p),p,0});\n    }\n    long long spent=0;\n    vector<int> bbList, routers;\n    vector<char> placed(N,0);\n    vector<int> q; q.reserve(N);\n    while(!pq.empty()){\n        if(B-spent<Pr) break;\n        E e=pq.top(); pq.pop();\n        int p=e.cell;\n        if(e.ver!=ver[p]||placed[p]) continue;\n        int gn=gainv[p]; if(gn<=0) continue;\n        long long cst=costOf(p);\n        double cur=(double)gn/cst;\n        if(cur<e.v*(1-1e-12)){ ver[p]++; pq.push({cur,p,ver[p]}); continue; }\n        if(spent+cst>B) continue;\n        if(1000LL*gn<=cst) continue;\n        // accept\n        spent+=cst; placed[p]=1; routers.push_back(p);\n        // backbone path\n        vector<int> path;\n        if(!isBB[p]){\n            int s=src[p]; int sr=s/W, sc=s%W; int r=p/W, c=p%W;\n            while(!(r==sr&&c==sc)){\n                path.push_back(r*W+c);\n                if(r<sr) r++; else if(r>sr) r--;\n                if(c<sc) c++; else if(c>sc) c--;\n            }\n            reverse(path.begin(),path.end());\n            for(int x:path){ isBB[x]=1; bbList.push_back(x); }\n        }\n        // coverage update\n        int pa=p/W, pbq=p%W;\n        forCover(pa,pbq,[&](int r,int l,int rr){\n            for(int c=l;c<=rr;c++){\n                int id=r*W+c;\n                if(g[r][c]=='.'&&!covered[id]){\n                    covered[id]=1;\n                    forCover(r,c,[&](int r2,int l2,int rr2){\n                        int base=r2*W;\n                        for(int c2=l2;c2<=rr2;c2++) gainv[base+c2]--;\n                    });\n                }\n            }\n        });\n        // BFS dist update\n        if(!path.empty()){\n            q.clear();\n            for(int x:path){ dist[x]=0; src[x]=x; q.push_back(x); if(gainv[x]>0&&!placed[x]){ver[x]++; pq.push({(double)gainv[x]/costOf(x),x,ver[x]});} }\n            size_t h=0;\n            while(h<q.size()){\n                int u=q[h++]; int ur=u/W, uc=u%W; int nd=dist[u]+1;\n                for(int dr=-1;dr<=1;dr++){ int vr=ur+dr; if(vr<0||vr>=H) continue;\n                    for(int dc=-1;dc<=1;dc++){ if(!dr&&!dc) continue; int vc=uc+dc; if(vc<0||vc>=W) continue;\n                        int v=vr*W+vc;\n                        if(dist[v]>nd){\n                            dist[v]=nd; src[v]=src[u]; q.push_back(v);\n                            if(gainv[v]>0&&!placed[v]&&g[vr][vc]!='#'){ ver[v]++; pq.push({(double)gainv[v]/costOf(v),v,ver[v]}); }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    string out;\n    out.reserve(32*(bbList.size()+routers.size())+64);\n    out+=to_string(bbList.size()); out+='\\n';\n    for(int x:bbList){ out+=to_string(x/W); out+=' '; out+=to_string(x%W); out+='\\n'; }\n    out+=to_string(routers.size()); out+='\\n';\n    for(int x:routers){ out+=to_string(x/W); out+=' '; out+=to_string(x%W); out+='\\n'; }\n    fwrite(out.data(),1,out.size(),stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
